      "text": "To find the first digit of the base 8 representation of \\(473_{10}\\), we need to convert the decimal number 473 to its base 8 equivalent. Here are the steps:\n\n1. **Determine the largest power of 8 that is less than or equal to 473:**\n   \\[\n   8^0 = 1, \\quad 8^1 = 8, \\quad 8^2 = 64, \\quad 8^3 = 512, \\quad 8^4 = 4096\n   \\]\n   Since \\(8^4 = 4096\\) is greater than 473, we use \\(8^3 = 512\\).\n\n2. **Divide 473 by 512:**\n   \\[\n   473 \\div 512 = 0 \\quad \\text{(quotient is 0)}\n   \\]\n   This means the coefficient for \\(8^3\\) is 0.\n\n3. **Remaining value after subtracting \\(512 \\times 0\\):**\n   \\[\n   473 - 512 \\times 0 = 473\n   \\]\n   Now, we need to divide 473 by the next lower power of 8, which is \\(8^2 = 64\\).\n\n4. **Divide 473 by 64:**\n   \\[\n   473 \\div 64 = 7 \\quad \\text{(quotient is 7)}\n   \\]\n   This means the coefficient for \\(8^2\\) is 7.\n\n5. **Remaining value after subtracting \\(64 \\times 7\\):**\n   \\[\n   473 - 64 \\times 7 = 473 - 448 = 25\n   \\]\n   Now, we need to divide 25 by the next lower power of 8, which is \\(8^1 = 8\\).\n\n6. **Divide 25 by 8:**\n   \\[\n   25 \\div 8 = 3 \\quad \\text{(quotient is 3)}\n   \\]\n   This means the coefficient for \\(8^1\\) is 3.\n\n7. **Remaining value after subtracting \\(8 \\times 3\\):**\n   \\[\n   25 - 8 \\times 3 = 25 - 24 = 1\n   \\]\n   Now, we need to divide 1 by the next lower power of 8, which is \\(8^0 = 1\\).\n\n8. **Divide 1 by 1:**\n   \\[\n   1 \\div 1 = 1 \\quad \\text{(quotient is 1)}\n   \\]\n   This means the coefficient for \\(8^0\\) is 1.\n\nPutting it all together, the base 8 representation of \\(473_{10}\\) is \\(731_8\\).\n\nTherefore, the first digit of the base 8 representation of \\(473_{10}\\) is \\(\\boxed{7}\\).",
